WEBVTT

00:00:05.673 --> 00:00:10.969
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Do you agree that people’s parenting styles are influenced by the way their parents brought them up?

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:17.140
<v><b>Tim:</b></v> I think it’s, er, it’s an interesting question and it’s a complicated one.

00:00:17.191 --> 00:00:21.689
Um, I think to an extent you are always going to be influenced by the way

00:00:21.714 --> 00:00:23.486
you were brought up yourself.

00:00:23.510 --> 00:00:27.020
Um, you might even react against the way that you were brought up.

00:00:27.105 --> 00:00:33.776
Er, I had a father who was a little bit distant, and so I think I’ve consciously tried to be, um,

00:00:33.801 --> 00:00:37.506
 closer and more physical with, with my own children.

00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:40.899
Um, but I think the environment has a huge part to play, as well.

00:00:40.924 --> 00:00:46.900
Um, and I’ve, I’ve had four children, er, sort of across a 20-year period,

00:00:46.928 --> 00:00:51.610
so two younger ones of eight and ten, and two older ones of 27 and 29, um,

00:00:52.027 --> 00:00:56.720
and I think I’ve brought them up in different ways according to, sort of,

00:00:56.738 --> 00:00:58.861
the times that, that we’ve lived in.

00:00:59.303 --> 00:01:04.085
Um, for example, my younger children are part of the digital age,

00:01:04.489 --> 00:01:09.265
and so it’s always a little bit of a tussle, a fight with them, to get them off screens.

00:01:09.693 --> 00:01:14.583
And with my 27-year-old and my 29-year-old, there were screens,

00:01:14.608 --> 00:01:17.149
but they weren’t that interesting and they weren’t on,

00:01:17.174 --> 00:01:19.100
they didn’t want to be on them the whole time.

00:01:19.125 --> 00:01:22.600
So it’s a, it’s a different sort of culture and a different environment.

00:01:22.995 --> 00:01:26.060
<v><b>Syinat:</b></v> Well, what you said about trying to be different to your parents…

00:01:26.085 --> 00:01:28.200
well, in, in areas that you didn’t really like,

00:01:28.474 --> 00:01:31.933
I think that at the end of the day we still replicate our parents exactly.

00:01:32.544 --> 00:01:35.040
Well, so, for example, my mother, when we were growing up,

00:01:35.065 --> 00:01:40.080
she always tried to make me see us as equals in, in the relationship and so,

00:01:40.306 --> 00:01:44.800
I definitely plan on doing that with my children as well…even if that is more of a positive thing.

00:01:44.819 --> 00:01:46.938
<v><b>Tim:</b></v> OK, that’s, that’s quite a different attitude.

00:01:46.954 --> 00:01:48.271
<v><b>Devika:</b></v> That’s…a very different attitude, yeah.

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:52.697
Um, I’ve seen a lot of my, sort of, people of my generation, so, cousins, for example,

00:01:52.722 --> 00:01:57.564
who’ve had kids, and seeing them bring them up, um, has been quite interesting.

00:01:57.589 --> 00:02:02.944
So, myself and, um, people of my generation were brought up in quite strict households

00:02:02.969 --> 00:02:05.333
and it’s been interesting, actually, to see, for example,

00:02:05.358 --> 00:02:09.367
one of my cousins is bringing up their children in a very different way, it’s very liberal,

00:02:09.878 --> 00:02:12.791
um, not really a good or bad thing it’s just very different, um…

00:02:12.815 --> 00:02:14.026
<v><b>Syinat:</b></v> Different priorities…

00:02:14.064 --> 00:02:14.725
<v><b>Devika:</b></v> Different priorities.

00:02:14.802 --> 00:02:17.918
But it is interesting to see that the core values at their parent,

00:02:17.934 --> 00:02:19.969
in their parenting haven’t really changed.

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:23.069
<v><b>Tim:</b></v> Right, OK, and is that partly, sort of, do,

00:02:23.094 --> 00:02:27.364
do you think they’ve chosen a different way of bringing them up, as a, as a reaction to…?

00:02:27.638 --> 00:02:31.141
<v><b>Devika:</b></v> I don’t know I think it’s actually an interesting combination of things,

00:02:31.166 --> 00:02:33.268
um, including the environment as you mentioned before.

00:02:33.318 --> 00:02:33.920
<v><b>Tim:</b></v> OK.